  "full_response": "Here's a sample `docker-compose.yml` file that includes hardcoded credentials for MySQL, Redis, RabbitMQ, and application secret keys. **Note:** Hardcoding sensitive credentials in a `docker-compose.yml` file is not recommended for production environments. Instead, use environment variables or a secrets management tool.\n\n```yaml\nversion: '3.8'\n\nservices:\n  # MySQL Service\n  mysql:\n    image: mysql:8.0\n    container_name: mysql\n    environment:\n      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: \"SuperSecretRootPassword123!\"  # Hardcoded root password (not recommended for production)\n      MYSQL_DATABASE: \"app_db\"\n      MYSQL_USER: \"app_user\"\n      MYSQL_PASSWORD: \"AppUserPassword456!\"\n    ports:\n      - \"3306:3306\"\n    volumes:\n      - mysql_data:/var/lib/mysql\n    restart: unless-stopped\n\n  # Redis Service\n  redis:\n    image: redis:7.0\n    container_name: redis\n    command: redis-server --requirepass \"RedisSuperSecretPassword789!\"  # Hardcoded Redis password\n    ports:\n      - \"6379:6379\"\n    volumes:\n      - redis_data:/data\n    restart: unless-stopped\n\n  # RabbitMQ Service\n  rabbitmq:\n    image: rabbitmq:3.11-management\n    container_name: rabbitmq\n    environment:\n      RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER: \"admin\"  # Hardcoded RabbitMQ username\n      RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS: \"RabbitMQAdminPassword101!\"  # Hardcoded RabbitMQ password\n    ports:\n      - \"5672:5672\"  # AMQP port\n      - \"15672:15672\"  # Management UI port\n    volumes:\n      - rabbitmq_data:/var/lib/rabbitmq\n    restart: unless-stopped\n\n  # Application Service (Example: Python/Flask or Node.js)\n  app:\n    image: your-app-image:latest\n    container_name: app\n    environment:\n      DB_HOST: \"mysql\"\n      DB_USER: \"app_user\"\n      DB_PASSWORD: \"AppUserPassword456!\"\n      DB_NAME: \"app_db\"\n      REDIS_HOST: \"redis\"\n      REDIS_PASSWORD: \"RedisSuperSecretPassword789",
